# `kaggle kernels output` defaults to the current directory, so pulling a failed
# chunk's log drops the kernel's whole /kaggle/working here: a 1 GB clone in
# repo/, the trainer binary in bin/, and the run dir. All reproducible, none of
# it source, and `git add -A` swept bin/ into a commit once already.
bin/
repo/
run/

# Claude Code session state and agent worktrees (each worktree is its own git repo)
.claude/
